, Mads","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anne","key":"duerpau","last":"Duer","name":"Duer, Anne","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mikael","key":"boesenpau","last":"Boesen","locid":"b449f652-d441-4b23-836f-2d5111ef64dd","name":"Boesen, Mikael","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kasper Kjaerulf","key":"gosvigpau","last":"Gosvig","name":"Gosvig, Kasper Kjaerulf","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jakob Mollenbach","key":"mollerpau","last":"Moller","name":"Moller, Jakob Mollenbach","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Niels Steen","key":"kroghpau","last":"Krogh","name":"Krogh, Niels Steen","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Bente","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Bente","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ole Rintek","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"69eac85e-ed5d-4571-86b1-7498674fffaf","name":"Madsen, Ole Rintek","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Jan","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Annette","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Annette","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"norregaardpau","last":"Norregaard","name":"Norregaard, Jesper","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"rogindpau","last":"Rogind","name":"Rogind, Henrik","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mikkel","key":"ostergaardpau","last":"Ostergaard","locid":"eb9b28bb-2658-4302-8342-2a662ef39d0c","name":"Østergaard, Mikkel","name_org":"Ostergaard, Mikkel","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34636846"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/rheumatology/keab755","issn":["14620324","14620332"],"issn_org":["14620324"],"issue":"6","journal":"Rheumatology","pages":"2398-2412","status":"p","title":"Rheumatology","volume":"61"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85131221586"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-33ad9c0d-e65f-4ca5-801c-7f5c0b84e3c7"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Tapering of TNF inhibitors in axial spondyloarthritis in routine care-2-year clinical and MRI outcomes and predictors of successful tapering","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-424172","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: To identify predictors of flare in a 2-year follow-up study of patients with rheumatoid arthritis (RA) in sustained clinical remission tapering towards withdrawal of biological disease-modifying anti-rheumatic drugs (bDMARDs). METHODS: Sustained clinical remission was defined as Disease Activity Score for 28 joints (DAS28)-C reactive protein (CRP) ≤2.6 without radiographic progression for >1 year. bDMARDs were tapered according to a mandatory clinical guideline to two-thirds of standard dose at baseline, half of dose at week 16 and discontinuation at week 32. Prospective assessments for 2 years included clinical evaluation, conventional radiography, ultrasound and MRI for signs of inflammation and bone changes. Flare was defined as DAS28-CRP ≥2.6 with ∆DAS28-CRP ≥1.2 from baseline. Baseline predictors of flare were assessed by logistic regression analyses. RESULTS: Of 142 included patients, 121 (85%) flared during follow-up of which 86% regained remission within 24 weeks after flare. Patients that flared were more often rheumatoid factor positive, had tried more bDMARDs and had higher baseline ultrasound synovitis sum scores than those not flaring. For patients on standard dose, predictors of flare within 16 weeks after reduction to two-thirds of standard dose were baseline MRI-osteitis (OR 1.16; 95% CI 1.03 to 1.33; p=0.014), gender (female) (OR 6.71; 95% CI 1.68 to 46.12; p=0.005) and disease duration (OR 1.06; 95% CI 1.01 to 1.11; p=0.020). Baseline predictors for flare within 2 years were ultrasound grey scale synovitis sum score (OR 1.19; 95% CI 1.02 to 1.44; p=0.020) and number of previous bDMARDs (OR 4.07; 95% CI 1.35 to 24.72; p=0.007). CONCLUSION: The majority of real-world patients with RA tapering bDMARDs flared during tapering, with the majority regaining remission after stepwise dose increase. Demographic and imaging parameters (MR-osteitis/ultrasound greyscale synovitis) were independent predictors of immediate flare and flare overall and may be of importance for clinical decision-making in patients eligible for tapering.","author_count":26,"contributors":["Terslev, Lene","Østergaard, Mikkel","Georgiadis, Stylianos","Brahe, Cecilie Heegaard","Ellegaard, Karen","Dohn, U. M.","Fana, Viktoria","Møller, Torsten","Juul, Lars","Huynh, Tuan Khai","Krabbe, Simon","Ornbjerg, L. M.","Glinatsi, Daniel","Røgind, Henrik","Hansen, Ann-Brit Eg","Nørregaard, Jesper","Jacobsen, Søren","Jensen, Dorte V.","Manilo, Natalia","Asmussen, Karsten","Boesen, Mikael","Rastiemadabadi, Zoreh","Morsel-Carlsen, Lone","Møller, Jakob Møllenbach","Krogh, Niels Steen","Hetland, Merete Lund"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-442269"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Skaraborgs Hospital Skövde"],"keyword":["Arthritis Rheumatoid","Inflammation","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Ultrasonography"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"flare during tapering of biological dmards in patients with rheumatoid arthritis in routine care characteristics and predictors","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/rmdopen-2022-002796","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-442269","identifier":[{"id":"36549857","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85144568565","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9791469","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-51c2b1f6-6eec-41d4-814e-8c17812bf126"],"keyword":["Magnetic Resonance Imaging","arthritis, rheumatoid","inflammation","ultrasonography"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0085A48DACF32B094C597E64F5B4F3FF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/rmdopen-2022-002796","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/341016534/e002796.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal Medicine: Rheumatology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"skaraborgs hospital skövde","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Skaraborgs Hospital Skövde","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"other hospitals","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-OTH","l3nl":"Other Hospitals","l3nn":"Other Hospitals","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Hospitals","namevar":["Capio Privathospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companie